---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { META, FACETS, NETWORK_LABELS } from '../lib/data';
import { fmt } from '../lib/seo';
---
<TextPage
	title="About eCamx | Live Cam Directory"
	description={`What eCamx is, how it works, and why it aggregates ${FACETS.networks.length} cam sites into one directory.`}
	heading="About eCamx"
>
	<p>
		eCamx is a live cam directory. It pulls the models who are broadcasting right
		now from {FACETS.networks.length} major webcam platforms and puts them in a
		single grid, so you can browse across all of them instead of keeping seven
		tabs open.
	</p>

	<h2>How it works</h2>
	<p>
		Once a day we fetch the public feeds from each platform, clean up the
		messy category labels they use, and rebuild the whole site as static pages.
		That is why it loads quickly and why there is nothing to sign up for.
		Who is online updates in your browser when the page loads.
	</p>
	<p>
		Right now the directory covers <strong>{fmt(META.modelCount)} models</strong> across
		{' '}{FACETS.categories.length} categories and {FACETS.countries.length} countries.
	</p>

	<h2>The platforms we cover</h2>
	<ul>
		{FACETS.networks.map((n) => (
			<li>
				<a href={`/site/${n.slug}/`}>{NETWORK_LABELS[n.slug]}</a>
				{' '}— {fmt(n.count)} models in the current index
			</li>
		))}
	</ul>

	<h2>What we are not</h2>
	<p>
		We do not run any of these platforms, we do not employ or represent any
		performer, and we host no video. Every stream plays through the originating
		platform's own player. If you spend money, you spend it there, not here.
	</p>

	<h2>How it pays for itself</h2>
	<p>
		Links out to the platforms carry an affiliate code. If you sign up or spend
		money after clicking through, we get a commission at no extra cost to you.
		That is the entire business model — no ads, no paywall, no data selling.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
		Broken listing, wrong data, or a removal request? See the
		<a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
	</p>
</TextPage>
